Subject: [PATCH] arm_neon: mark the assembly stack non-executable

None of the hand-written ARM files (modules/arm_neon/*.S and
video_filter/deinterlace/merge_arm.S, which all include asm.S) has a
.note.GNU-stack section, so the linker assumes they need an executable
stack and marks every plugin built from them GNU_STACK RWE. Since glibc
2.41 dlopen() no longer makes the stack executable and refuses such a
library ("cannot enable executable stack as shared object requires"):
the NEON chroma, volume and channel mixer plugins and the deinterlace
filter never load.

Add the note in asm.S. No function in these files runs code from the
stack.

Found on the Powkiddy A12 (RK3128, Cortex-A7, glibc 2.44) with cvlc -vv.
--- a/modules/arm_neon/asm.S
+++ b/modules/arm_neon/asm.S
@@ -30,6 +30,14 @@
 #   define HAVE_AS_FPU_DIRECTIVE  1
 #endif
 
+#ifdef __ELF__
+/* No hand-written function here needs an executable stack: say so, or the
+ * linker marks every plugin built from these files GNU_STACK RWE and glibc
+ * (2.41 and later) refuses to dlopen() it. */
+	.pushsection .note.GNU-stack,"",%progbits
+	.popsection
+#endif
+
 .macro  function name
 	.globl  EXTERN_ASM\name
 #ifdef __ELF__
